E=[('Redline 14 · when God is stripped out', 130, 'Strip God out of the picture and "good" slowly shrinks to *usefulness* — what a life can produce, contribute, or enjoy — and once that happens, any person can be weighed, traded, or spent for a larger sum, because all such standards are ultimately set by human beings and therefore can be revised by human beings.', 'Strip God out of the picture and "good" has no fixed meaning. People decide it for themselves: usefulness, pleasure, whatever the majority wants. And once people decide what is good, they can also decide that some people are worth less, because a standard made by human beings can be changed by human beings.')]
